Z||000000||costly86gt||07-04-2000||10:17 PM||||I have an 86 gt and was wondering how to remove the molding on the car without breaking it?Also how can I get the rocker panels off?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||07-04-2000||11:51 PM||||I know about the moldings.  Just had to take them off of my 86 GT.  What you do is this:  start in the front.  Take out the 7mm nut holding the piece on.  After it is out, put your thumbs (use both hands) at the bottom.  Pull up with your thumbs.  I had to use a small-bladed standard screwdriver to pry up the bottom of the molding on some pieces.  You can skip the front fascia if you want; did on mine.  On the door, just pull up; no nuts holding the molding on.  I also skipped the piece of molding behind the door handle.  On the piece behind the door, take out the 7mm nut.  Start on the BACK of the molding and pry up.  When you get up to the back of the door and when the molding is removed, pull toward the front of the Fiero to remove the rivets.  Prying might also be necessary.  Finally, on the back molding, you can't take it out because it is all one part of the rear fascia.  ||||reg||10
